      en: "The Parliament building in Tbilisi on Rustaveli Avenue is the seat of Georgia's parliament. Built in the 1930s in Socialist Classicism style, it originally housed the Georgian Central Committee. After independence, it was renovated. The structure features a colonnaded facade and a large domed hall. It witnessed historic events, including the 2003 Rose Revolution. Though a new parliament building was built in Kutaisi, the Tbilisi building still houses some committees.",
