      en: "Samtavro Monastery in Mtskheta, Georgia, is a key religious complex founded in the 4th century by King Mirian III after Georgia's Christianization. The main Samtavro Church was built in the 11th century, featuring a cross-in-square plan and a central dome. The monastery also includes the Convent of St. Nino, honoring the evangelizer of Georgia. It served as a royal necropolis for early Georgian kings. The 15th-century belfry is a notable architectural addition. The site is part of the UNESCO World Heritage Site of Mtskheta. Today, it functions as an active nunnery, attracting pilgrims and tourists. The interior frescoes, largely from the 19th century, depict scenes from the life of Christ and Georgian saints.",
