      en: "Motsameta Monastery, perched on a cliff above the Tsqaltitela River near Kutaisi, Georgia, dates back to the 11th century. It honors the 8th-century martyrs David and Constantine, brothers executed by Arabs for refusing to convert to Islam. The church is a small cross-in-square plan with a dome, featuring 16th-century frescoes depicting the brothers' martyrdom. A unique tradition involves pilgrims crawling three times around the church to make a wish, believed to bring luck. The monastery offers breathtaking views of the Rioni River gorge. It underwent restoration in the 19th century and remains an active religious site, attracting both worshippers and tourists interested in Georgian medieval architecture and legends.",
