      en: "Nokalakevi, also called Archaeopolis, is an ancient city in western Georgia (Samegrelo). It served as the capital of the Kingdom of Colchis and later Lazica. The settlement dates back to the 4th century BC and was inhabited until the medieval period. Ruins include city walls, towers, palaces, and bathhouses from Hellenistic and Roman times. Excavations have uncovered mosaics, coins, and pottery. It was a key trading post on the Silk Road. In the 6th century, it was contested between Byzantium and Persia. Today, it is an open-air archaeological museum, revealing layers of Georgian history.",
